@startuml
' OWNER-MVP-2026-11-04 review: Method / document navigation. Scope-independent process/navigation; provider or runner examples are not MVP prerequisites.
 title Resumefolio - Change assessment and decision recording
skinparam backgroundColor white
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam defaultFontSize 14
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam activity {
  BackgroundColor #DBEAFE
  BorderColor #94A3B8
  FontColor #17324D
  DiamondBackgroundColor #FEF3C7
  DiamondBorderColor #94A3B8
  StartColor #17324D
  EndColor #17324D
}
start
:Describe the change and its reason;
:Assess affected artifacts, effort, cost, quality,\noperations, dependencies, risks and alternatives;
if (Changes agreed scope, spending or delivery commitments?) then (yes)
  :Obtain an explicit project-owner decision;
  if (Accepted?) then (yes)
    :Record decision, rationale, date and follow-up;
  else (rejected or deferred)
    :Record outcome and reasons; do not apply the proposal;
    stop
  endif
else (within agreed boundaries)
  :Proceed within existing authorization;\nrecord significant technical rationale where relevant;
endif
:Update affected work, documents and diagrams;
:Perform relevant verification and review results;
:Record a focused Git checkpoint;
stop
legend bottom
Content approval is distinct from system-required execution permissions.
A commit is not milestone completion, publication or release approval.
Product coding still requires the agreed pre-implementation baseline.
endlegend
@enduml
